    "answer": "one-place/(all-in)-the-same-place/one-spot/one-location/one-part/one-passage",
    "mnemonic": "Remember the small ヶ acting as a counter? Together with <kanji>one</kanji> and <kanji>place</kanji>, it makes this <vocabulary>one place</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>one spot</vocabulary>.\n\nJust like 〜ヶ月, you'll also run into this being written as 一箇所, 一か所, or 一カ所.",
    "readingMnemonic": "Just like before, the little ヶ is actually read as か. The rest uses the on'yomi you already learned with the kanji. Just watch out 一 here is いっ instead of いち as it makes it easier to pronounce the whole word. Now, read it aloud and try yourself!",
